# The writing stage's endpoint - app/llm/client.py.
# Loaded by api/app/config.py on every LLM call, so an edit lands on the next round
# without a restart. A real environment variable always wins over this file.
#
#   CH_LLM_BASE_URL         the OpenAI-compatible gateway, e.g.
#                           https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1
#   CH_LLM_API_KEY          one or more keys, comma-separated. The first is the primary;
#                           the rest are standbys, tried in order when the one before it
#                           refuses with 401, 402, 403 or 429 (dead credential, drained
#                           account, exhausted quota). A key that refuses is skipped for
#                           CH_LLM_KEY_COOLDOWN seconds, so a dead primary is paid for
#                           once per round instead of once per call.
#   CH_LLM_API_KEY_FALLBACK standbys, comma-separated, appended after CH_LLM_API_KEY.
#                           Either variable alone is enough; this one is here so a key
#                           can be added without editing the primary line.
#   CH_LLM_MODEL            the model the gateway expects
#   CH_LLM_TIMEOUT          seconds for one call, default 180
#   CH_LLM_MAX_TOKENS       the answer ceiling. A reasoning model bills its thinking
#                           against it, so a tight one comes back empty with
#                           finish_reason=length instead of an error. 0 = leave it unset.
#   CH_LLM_REASONING        how hard the model may think before it answers: none /
#                           minimal / low / medium / high. Only none is a real switch:
#                           minimal and low still spent 680-899 thinking tokens where
#                           none spent 0. Set to none and pair it with the repair pass -
#                           five tokens took 94.9s and kept 5/5 against 340.1s and 4/5 on
#                           the endpoint default, with more prose rather than less.
#   CH_LLM_TRIES            attempts per key while the failure looks transient, default 2.
#                           With a timeout above the real answer time this only doubles a
#                           stall: 180s x 2 made one dead call cost 366s of a 421s stage.
#   CH_LLM_KEY_COOLDOWN     seconds a refused key is skipped, default 600. 0 disables it.
#   CH_LLM_EXTRA_HEADERS    a JSON object of headers the gateway wants, e.g.
#                           {"x-opencode-session": "crypto-hunter"}
#   CH_RESEARCH_WORKERS     how many tokens one reading pass researches at the same time,
#                           default 12. It gates the model calls only; the links were already
#                           found at their own width. Turn it down first if the provider
#                           starts answering 429.
#
# Note that the whole key list lives in one variable: a real CH_LLM_API_KEY in the
# environment replaces the file's, standbys included, so put either all of them in the
# environment or all of them here.

# Copy this file to llm.env and fill it in.
CH_LLM_BASE_URL=
CH_LLM_API_KEY=
CH_LLM_API_KEY_FALLBACK=
CH_LLM_MODEL=
CH_LLM_TIMEOUT=300
CH_LLM_MAX_TOKENS=0
CH_LLM_TRIES=1
CH_LLM_REASONING=none
CH_LLM_KEY_COOLDOWN=600
CH_LLM_EXTRA_HEADERS=
CH_RESEARCH_WORKERS=12
